    // The full jar is NOT added as runtimeOnly. Tested, and the result is the same dead end as
    // with Curios, just one step further: put by hand in runClient/mods, Patchouli dies on
    // startup calling Minecraft.m_91087_() (the SRG name of getInstance) from its
    // BookCrashHandler; passed through fg.deobf, that call is fixed but its mixins fail, and
    // enabling mixin.env.remapRefMap to fix them breaks the mixins of any other production mod with
    // mixins loaded in the same client —Citadel the first one when it was tried—.
    // A development client cannot have deobfuscated mods and production mods with
    // mixins at the same time, and that is why runClient/mods stays empty (see above).
    //
    // So the Patchouli Guide is tested in a normal install with the built jar. What
    // is checked here is its structure: checkPatchouliBook requires every page of the Guide to be
    // in exactly one entry of the book, in both directions.

    // The full jar is NOT added as runtimeOnly, even though it would be handy for testing the integration:
    // Curios is published with its mixins referencing SRG names (f_19803_), and runClient runs with
    // parchment mappings, where that name doesn't exist. The result is that the development client doesn't
    // start — tested with 5.14.1 and with 5.4.7, so it is not version drift but the environment's
    // remapping. Making it work would require configuring mixin refmap remapping, and the only thing it
    // would buy is being able to test Curios locally: the integration itself is structurally isolated
    // (see CuriosCompat) and is verified with javap, not by running it. To really test it, a
    // real install, not a development environment.
}

// The manifest is NOT decoration: mods.toml declares version="${file.jarVersion}", and that marker is
// resolved by Forge reading Implementation-Version from HERE. Without this line, the mod announces itself in-game
// with the literal text "${file.jarVersion}". It goes in both jars because the one that is published is the shadow.
// The value is captured HERE and not inside the closure: inside manifest{} the delegate is the Manifest, not
// the task, so archiveVersion doesn't resolve — it fails when evaluating the script, not when packaging.
def modVersion = project.version.toString()
def modManifest = {
    attributes(['Implementation-Version': modVersion])
}

jar {
    archiveClassifier = 'slim'
    manifest modManifest
}

shadowJar {
    archiveClassifier = ''
    configurations = [project.configurations.shade]
    relocate 'io.github.tfriedrichs.dicebot', "${project.group}.relocated.dicebot"
    manifest modManifest
